1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,852
Mother... let the world... light lamps for me.

2
00:00:04,202 --> 00:00:08,879
A demon's last wish... is why we light lamps on Diwali.

3
00:00:09,129 --> 00:00:11,302
A demon wanted lamps, Paati?

4
00:00:11,652 --> 00:00:20,226
Listen, kanna. Narakasura, son of Mother Earth, had a boon. No one could kill him... except his own mother.

5
00:00:20,576 --> 00:00:26,565
Drunk on power, he spread darkness... and locked away sixteen thousand women.

6
00:00:26,915 --> 00:00:32,666
So Krishna came, with Queen Satyabhama... Mother Earth herself, born again.

7
00:00:33,016 --> 00:00:38,738
In battle, Krishna stepped back... and smiled. This fight was hers.

8
00:00:39,088 --> 00:00:41,502
Your darkness ends today, Naraka!

9
00:00:41,852 --> 00:00:43,517
Mother...?

10
00:00:43,767 --> 00:00:49,698
With his last breath, he knew her. And he asked for only one thing... light.

11
00:00:50,048 --> 00:00:55,006
At dawn, the prisoners walked free... and every home lit a lamp.

12
00:00:55,356 --> 00:00:57,950
So even darkness wished for light...

13
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:04,120
No darkness is so deep that one small lamp cannot end it. Happy Diwali, kanna.

